"Grillon champêtre":"Field cricket","Grillon":"Cricket","Ver luisant":"Glow-worm","Chanteur, détritivore":"Singer, detritivore","La litière, les graines, les cadavres, parfois une jeune pousse.":"Leaf litter, seeds, corpses, sometimes a young shoot.","Le scorpion, la mante, les araignées chasseuses, la scolopendre.":"The scorpion, the mantis, hunting spiders, the centipede.","Recycle les débris ; son chant anime les nuits du vivarium.":"Recycles debris; its song livens up the vivarium's nights.","Un abri pour la journée (pierre, écorce), un sol sec en surface.":"A shelter for the day (stone, bark), dry soil on the surface.","Caché le jour, il sort la nuit. Le mâle chante en frottant ses ailes l'une contre l'autre. La femelle pond dans le sol avec sa longue tarière ; les petits ressemblent aux adultes, sans ailes.":"Hidden by day, it comes out at night. The male sings by rubbing its wings together. The female lays in the soil with her long ovipositor; the young look like the adults, without wings.",
"Chasseur d'escargots, lumineux":"Snail hunter, glowing","Les escargots surtout ; à défaut, les cadavres.":"Mostly snails; failing that, corpses.","Le scorpion, la scolopendre.":"The scorpion, the centipede.","Empêche les escargots de tout dévorer.":"Stops snails from devouring everything.","De l'humidité, des escargots, un coin sombre.":"Moisture, snails, a dark corner.","C'est un coléoptère : la femelle, sans ailes, ressemble à une larve. La nuit, le bout de son ventre s'allume d'une lumière vert-jaune froide pour attirer les mâles. Sa larve paralyse les escargots d'une morsure.":"It is a beetle: the wingless female looks like a larva. At night, the tip of her abdomen lights up with a cold yellow-green glow to attract males. Its larva paralyses snails with a bite.",
"Une femelle grillon pond dans le sol":"A female cricket lays eggs in the soil","Un ver luisant a eu un escargot":"A glow-worm got a snail","larve de coccinelle":"ladybird larva","nymphe de coccinelle":"ladybird pupa","pupe de mouche":"fly pupa","Larve de coccinelle":"Ladybird larva","Nymphe de coccinelle":"Ladybird pupa","Pupe de mouche":"Fly pupa","Asticot":"Maggot","Une larve de coccinelle":"A ladybird larva","Une nymphe de coccinelle":"A ladybird pupa","Un asticot":"A maggot","Une pupe de mouche":"A fly pupa",
"🍄 Le sol reste détrempé : un champignon rend une bête malade. Aère ou laisse sécher.":"🍄 The soil stays soaked: a fungus makes a creature sick. Ventilate or let it dry.","Bataille entre deux colonies de fourmis":"Battle between two ant colonies","Plante surpeuplée : des pucerons ailés s'envolent":"Overcrowded plant: winged aphids fly off","🦂 Petit scorpion, sur le dos de sa mère":"🦂 Baby scorpion, on its mother's back","🐛 Larve : dévore les pucerons, puis se fixera en nymphe":"🐛 Larva: devours aphids, then will settle as a pupa","🐛 Asticot : se nourrit, puis deviendra une pupe":"🐛 Maggot: feeding, then will become a pupa","⏳ Nymphe immobile : se transforme en adulte":"⏳ Still pupa: turning into an adult","🪽 Puceron ailé : part fonder une colonie sur une autre plante":"🪽 Winged aphid: off to found a colony on another plant","🍄 Malade : un champignon l'affaiblit (sol trop humide)":"🍄 Sick: a fungus is weakening it (soil too wet)","🎶 Chante pour attirer une femelle":"🎶 Singing to attract a female","✨ S'allume pour attirer un partenaire":"✨ Glowing to attract a mate","🐌 Traque un escargot":"🐌 Stalking a snail","🍼 Jeune, il grandit":"🍼 Young, growing","👴 Âgé, plus lent":"👴 Old, slower",
